            { q: "Based on the paired passages, what is one key similarity and one key difference between the two authors' views?", p: "Passage 1 argues that social media has strengthened democracy by giving ordinary citizens a platform to organize and share information. Passage 2 acknowledges that social media can spread misinformation quickly, but argues that overall it has increased political participation among young people. Both authors cite surveys showing increased online political activity, but Passage 1 emphasizes benefits while Passage 2 emphasizes risks alongside benefits.", a: ["Both authors oppose social media", "Both see increased participation, but differ on whether benefits outweigh risks", "The authors completely disagree", "Neither author provides evidence"], c: 1, explanation: "Both authors note increased political participation, but Passage 1 focuses on benefits while Passage 2 balances benefits with risks.", passage_title: "Social Media and Democracy", a_explanations: ["Incorrect. Both authors see benefits.", "Correct! Both note participation increases but differ on risk-benefit balance.", "Incorrect. They agree on participation but differ on overall assessment.", "Incorrect. Both cite survey evidence."], hint: "What do both authors agree on, and where do they differ?" }
